              "answer_markdown": "Moderna's investment case, as kept in the Zopedia MRNA business memory dated 14 October 2026, is a funded move away from vaccine sales at pandemic scale toward a wider respiratory vaccine line and an oncology programme. The money shows both the strain and the support: revenue fell from $1.016 billion in 2025Q3 to $145 million in 2026Q2, with a $782 million net loss and -$563 million of free cash flow, while cash was $6.9 billion at 30 June 2026 and management guides to $4.7\u20135.2 billion at year-end 2026. The replacement products are Spikevax and mNEXSPIKE for COVID-19, mRESVIA for RSV, mFLUSIVA (approved 5 August 2026), and the Merck-partnered intismeran autogene, which met Phase 3 endpoints in resected melanoma in August 2026; the retamed research rests on the Q2 2026 report for the quarter ended 30 June 2026 plus news through 13 October 2026, and the next hard check is Q3 2026 results on 6 November 2026.",
              "engine_revision": "12045e007003b2833584",
              "evidence_pack_id": "aqlpack::c3ffca56b02a67a057d609a3"
            },
            "write_policy": "none"
          },
