              "quality_review": {
                "status": "completed",
                "verdict": "revise"
              },
              "answer_markdown": "The operating thesis is unchanged: Moderna is using a funded balance sheet to move away from pandemic-scale vaccine sales toward a wider respiratory vaccine line and the Merck-partnered oncology treatment intismeran autogene; on a like-for-like basis, Q2 2026 revenue of $145 million was about 2% above the $142 million reported a year earlier, so the yearly level was roughly flat (Moderna Q2 2026 release). Revenue fell from quarter to quarter, from $1.016 billion in 2025Q3 to $678 million in 2025Q4, $389 million in 2026Q1 and $145 million in 2026Q2, and because management says about 55% of second-half 2026 revenue will fall in the third quarter, a Q3 2026 rise over Q2 2026 would cross seasons and show expected timing, not proof of recovery; the 6 November 2026 report is the next hard check.",
